<title>USA: First USA sells $200 million of debt.</title>
<headline>First USA sells $200 million of debt.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>First USA Inc said on Friday it has sold $200 million of non-convertible capital securities from First USA Capital Trust I, a newly formed Delaware business trust.</p>
<p>The 9.33 percent capital securities were priced at par to yield 260 basis points above the 30-year Treasury, First USA said.</p>
<p>Cash distributions will be payable semi-annually beginning July 15, 1997, the company said. Proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes.</p>
</text>
